# TanStack Form

`Label`, `Input`, and `Textarea` are UI only. Do not import `@tanstack/react-form` inside `app/shared/ui/`. Do not replace them with raw `<input>`, `<textarea>`, or `<label>`.

## Reuse

- Field schemas live in `app/shared/lib/schemas.ts`. Add `email`, `password`, `npi`, `city`, and similar fields there once, then pass them as `validate`.
- Compose longer forms with `z.object({ email: emailSchema, city: citySchema })`.
- Text inputs use `FormInput` from `@/shared/lib/FormInput`. Do not copy `form.Field` + `Label` + `Input` by hand.
- Checkboxes, OTP, and other non-input controls stay on `form.Field` (or their own component).

## Validate

- Run schemas on `onBlur` and `onSubmit` (this is what `FormInput` does).
- Do not validate on every keystroke from the start. After an error is showing, clear it when the value becomes valid (`revalidateIfError`).
- Use `error` on both `Label` and the field. Show the first message as `helperText`. `FormInput` already does this.

```tsx
<FormInput
  form={form}
  label="Email address"
  name="email"
  type="email"
  validate={emailSchema}
/>
```

Do not spread the TanStack `field` object onto `Input` or `Textarea`.
